From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_interface: let the build turn the source interface check
 on

The firmware finds a connection by its 5-tuple alone. A flow that crosses
the box twice - a guest client behind an access point reaching a device
on the LAN behind the same access point, through a router on the shared
uplink - is bridged in the guest VLAN on the way out and in the LAN VLAN
on the way back. Once the first leg is accelerated, the packet of the
second leg matches its rule and is sent out of the uplink again, with the
L2 header it arrived with.

net.ecm.src_interface_check makes the front end set the SRC_INTERFACE_CHECK
flag on every rule: the firmware then hands a packet that arrives on
another interface than the rule's to the host and drops the rule. It is
off by default and can only be turned on once the module is loaded, when
the first rules may already be in the firmware - and one packet forwarded
the wrong way is enough.

Let the build choose the initial value. The sysctl works as before.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
diff -urN a/ecm_interface.c b/ecm_interface.c
--- a/ecm_interface.c	2026-10-10 17:00:21.537634334 +0200
+++ b/ecm_interface.c	2026-10-10 17:00:21.553634654 +0200
@@ -203,8 +203,14 @@
  * Source interface check flag.
  *	If it is enabled, the acceleration engine will check the flow's interface to see
  *	whether it matches with the rule's source interface or not.
+ *
+ *	The build can turn it on from the start (ECM_INTERFACE_SRC_CHECK_DEFAULT);
+ *	net.ecm.src_interface_check still changes it at run time.
  */
-int ecm_interface_src_check;
+#ifndef ECM_INTERFACE_SRC_CHECK_DEFAULT
+#define ECM_INTERFACE_SRC_CHECK_DEFAULT 0
+#endif
+int ecm_interface_src_check = ECM_INTERFACE_SRC_CHECK_DEFAULT;
 
 /*
  * Sysctl to enable mwan3
